return PlaceObj('ModDef', {
	'title', "The Nests Awaken!",
	'description', '[h1] A new disaster looms![/h1]\n[h3]A crumb of new content for these thirsting for more.[/h3]\n\n[h2]The nests will now realize that you are a threat, and must be cleansed![/h2]\n\nThis mod adds:\n1. New mechanics for nests (Shrieker, Scissorhand, and a new Consortium "Nest") that "learns" about the players presence.\n1a. They now consume nearby resources slowly (Unless awoken). To do what? Create more & Evolve their defenders!\n1b. If awoken, those defenders will instead be attacking you!\n\n2. A new looming disaster where a single species attempts world domination!\nThe specific species is semi-random, and there is a semi-hidden way for you to pick the one you want.\n\n3. Four new expedition sites (One for each nest species and a special bonus one) that can be found while exploring. Each with 3 different event chains with negative and positive results! With each event having the ability to influence the nests on the game map.\n\n4. Totally unrelated (I promise) there is a new reward type from expeditions, Tamed animals! Now you can convince and bring home "friends" from afar.\n\n5. Mod settings to set how you want notifications about nearby nests.\n\nBut be warned awoken nests are [b]much[/b] harder to kill.\n\nYour difficulty choice greatly influences how to end the disaster, how fast the nests grow and send attacks, and a few other misc things.\n\n[h3]Plans:[/h3]\nI plan to develop for this mod:\n- New nest types (Shogu, Camel, etc...)\n- Species specific rewards for fending off the disaster\n- More expeditions or events that let you interact with the flora/fauna of the planet\n\n[b]This mod does heavily use and rely on Enemys Evolve mod[\\b]',
	'image', "Mod/TGkJ3Tu/Pics Or it Didn't Happen/Shrieker_Nest_small.png",
	'last_changes', 'Update 1.5 bugs, bugs, bugs, some qol, and some more bugs\n\n#1 Bugfix: Stopped units from spawning underneath their nests (Leading to nasty surprises post nest kill)\n\n#2 Bugfix: Re-added code that made sure Consortium nest robots will spawn aggressive to player\n(Oops I did it again, I accidentally removed and had to re-add it back) (To the tune of Brittney Spears I did it again)\n\n#3 Bugfix: Enemy Consortium nest robots will never flee attacks. A "free" bug discovered after re-fixing #2\n\n#4 Bugfix: Enemy Consortium nest attacks against the player now will walk and attack the players stuff instead of just standing there\n\n#5 Bugfix: The nest tutorial will now only show up once per save.\n(I shifted that and other save game specific flags to be stored/fetched in accordance with how the base game does it)\n\n#6 New Mod Option: Option to set the max # of each species allowed. \nThis by default 13, but can be set from anywhere from 8 to 20.\n\n#7 QoL: Nests now have an additional bar indicating how strong their next attack will be.\nIf the attack is going to be at or above the players score, the indicator will change to a more ominous visual\n\n#8 QoL: The nest UI bar indicating how quickly the next attack will occur now obfuscates the last 10% progress.\nAnd the render is now a more ominous "imminment" with a full bar; until the attack occurs.\n\n#9 Bugfix: Changed the math on how powerful nest attacks are.\nTL:DR Nests now have much stricter caps on how powerful of an attack they can send.\n\n#10 QoL: Nests no longer count "attacks" sent without being alerted to the player in attack score\n\n#11 QoL: Nests that release "attack" w/o being alerted to the players presence will no longer cause the "enemies attacking" notification.\n\n#12 Nest Rebalance: Nests when attacking the player will now grant the units a movement speed buff.\nThis is to help them get to the player before they despawn.\nThe speed gain will be higher the farther away the center of the players colony the units are, and will fall off when they get in range.\n(This may be computationally expensive, so this may be removed in the near future)\n\nGeneral notes to explain this update and the state of the mod:\nAttack Caps:\nA nest attacks minimum strength is 30% player score. \n(Normal attacks are almost always at 100% player score)\n\nThere are now multiple layers enforcing caps on how strong a nest attack can be.\nCap #1. Attack cap increases by 10% per alert nests on the map of that species.\nCap #2. 50% per year\nExamples: \na. 10 alert nests in year 1, each nest will only send a 50% strength attack at you. (Cap #2 in effect)\nb. 9 alert nests in year 2, the cap will be 90% . (Cap #1 in effect)\n\nAttack Strength:\nNests gain attack strength from the following:\n- Base strength of 20%\n- Difficulty setting of game (+0 on low, +10 on higher diffs)\n- How many times this nest has attacked before (+10% per attack, reset when the nest evolves it\'s brood)\n- "Banked" aggression, which are times the species wanted to generate a nest but couldn\'t (+10% per, reset after first attack of species)\n- Nests lose 20% attack strength per stack of movement speed they must give to their units. \nThis means that nests farther away will attack with weaker forces generally, unless they are over-capped on attack strength.\nAny issues with this.... very complex mod please include the logs so I can track down why.',
